diff -ruN '--exclude=OUR_CHANGES*.md' a/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_16os.topo b/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_16os.topo
--- a/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_16os.topo	1969-12-31 19:00:00.000000000 -0500
+++ b/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_16os.topo	2026-11-07 23:32:37.774774027 -0500
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Spine-starved variant of rail_128_1os.topo: same 8 rail (leaf) switches of
+# 16 hosts, but ONE spine and one 100 Gbps uplink per rail switch (16:1).
+# The .topo format cannot remove the spine entirely (radix_up must be > 0
+# below the top tier, fat_tree_topology.cpp:276), so this is the closest
+# expressible stand-in for Wang et al.'s rail-only network: cross-rail
+# capacity is 1/16 of rail-optimized. Rail-local traffic (rail labelling,
+# host = 16*gpu_index + node) never touches the spine and should be
+# unaffected. See docs/TOPOLOGY_RAIL.md.
+Nodes 128
+Tiers 2
+Podsize 128
+
+Tier 0
+Oversubscribed 16
+Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
+Radix_Down 16
+Radix_Up 1
+Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
+Switch_Latency_ns 0
+
+Tier 1
+Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
+Radix_Down 8
+Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
+Switch_Latency_ns 0
diff -ruN '--exclude=OUR_CHANGES*.md' a/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_1os.topo b/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_1os.topo
--- a/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_1os.topo	1969-12-31 19:00:00.000000000 -0500
+++ b/htsim/sim/datacenter/topologies/rail_128_1os.topo	2026-11-07 23:32:37.774785719 -0500
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Rail-optimized fabric for 16 HGX nodes x 8 GPUs = 128 NICs (Wang et al.,
+# arXiv 2307.12169, Fig. 1/3 "rail-optimized"), expressed as a 2-tier
+# leaf-spine. Physical graph: 8 leaf (= rail) switches with 16 host ports and
+# 16 uplinks each, 16 spines with one link to every leaf, 100 Gbps, 1:1.
+#
+# HTSIM wires host h to leaf h/16 (fat_tree_topology.h HOST_POD_SWITCH).
+# The graph is the same as an ordinary 128-host leaf-spine; what makes it
+# rail-optimized is the host labelling used in the traffic matrix:
+#   rail labelling          host = 16*gpu_index + node   (leaf i = rail i)
+#   conventional labelling  host = 8*node + gpu_index    (leaf = 2 nodes)
+# See docs/TOPOLOGY_RAIL.md.
+Nodes 128
+Tiers 2
+Podsize 128
+
+Tier 0
+Oversubscribed 1
+Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
+Radix_Down 16
+Radix_Up 16
+Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
+Switch_Latency_ns 0
+
+Tier 1
+Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
+Radix_Down 8
+Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
+Switch_Latency_ns 0
